---
// Floating "Back to Services" pill -- only rendered on
// /foundation-repair-methods and the 8 method pages linked from it (via
// Layout's `backToServices` prop). Exists because the sitewide prev/next
// chevrons (MobilePageFlowNav) chain straight through all 8 method pages
// in nav order, so from the middle of that chain "prev" steps to the
// previous method page, not back to Services -- not what someone who
// followed a "Read the full technical breakdown" link actually wants.
// Unlike the other floating buttons this isn't scroll-gated: the need to
// back out can hit the moment someone lands, not just after scrolling.
---

<a href="/foundation-repair-methods" id="tls-back-to-services" aria-label="Back to Foundation Repair Methods">
  <span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Services
</a>

<style>
  #tls-back-to-services {
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 28px;
    left: 20px;
    height: 44px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    background: var(--blue);
    color: #fff;
    border: 2px solid var(--gold);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    z-index: 9999;
    box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(13, 34, 56, 0.45);
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }
  #tls-back-to-services:hover {
    background: var(--gold);
  }
  /* Sitewide footer-visibility observer, see Layout.astro. */
  body.tls-footer-visible #tls-back-to-services {
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  /* PageSummary's pill takes the mobile left:20/bottom:28 slot -- stack
     this one above it there instead of overlapping. Desktop keeps this
     slot to itself (Summary sits at right:192 on desktop). */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    #tls-back-to-services {
      bottom: 84px;
    }
  }
</style>
